- @meet_candidates: Meet the eleven candidates

@meet_candidates
title: Eleven candidates, seven electoral fields
on-arrival: pres_candidate_tour_seen = 1

Only the two strongest candidates will advance to the runoff. Lewica's nominee
begins outside those leading positions, but the first round still matters: a
credible result can establish the Left as an independent force, push its issues
into the national campaign and determine what either finalist must offer to
win over its voters.

Before choosing our strategy, we should examine the candidates and the
electorates each hopes to mobilise.

- @candidate_duda: First, the incumbent

@candidate_duda
title: Andrzej Duda — the incumbent
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-duda.webp

**Andrzej Duda — President of Poland, backed by PiS and the United Right**

PiS presents Duda as the guarantor of continuity: social transfers,
conservative institutions and a presidency working in step with the
government. He begins with the largest disciplined electorate and the full
machinery of the governing camp behind him.

His danger is that the election becomes a verdict on the government's handling
of the pandemic and its failed attempt to force through the May vote.

- @candidate_trzaskowski: KO changed its candidate

@candidate_trzaskowski
title: Rafał Trzaskowski — the late challenger
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-trzaskowski.webp

**Rafał Trzaskowski — Warsaw mayor and KO's replacement candidate**

After Małgorzata Kidawa-Błońska withdraws, Warsaw's mayor enters a shortened
campaign and rapidly rebuilds KO's liberal and metropolitan electorate. He
offers opposition voters a direct institutional challenge to PiS rather than
another attempt to escape the two-bloc contest.

A Trzaskowski victory would place an opposition president above a PiS cabinet.
Vetoes, judicial appointments and the constitutional limits of cohabitation
would become the next political battlefield.

- @candidate_holownia: Now the outsider

@candidate_holownia
title: Szymon Hołownia — the outsider
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia.webp

**Szymon Hołownia — independent publicist and television presenter**

Hołownia asks voters exhausted by the PiS–KO conflict to leave both established
camps behind. His campaign combines moderate social language, institutional
reform and a volunteer organisation without an existing parliamentary party.

Even if he misses the runoff, those volunteers and voters may become the basis
of a durable new centrist movement.

- @candidate_bosak: Konfederacja has made its choice

@candidate_bosak
title: Krzysztof Bosak — the radical-right organiser
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-bosak.webp

**Krzysztof Bosak — Konfederacja MP and National Movement organiser**

Bosak gives Konfederacja a disciplined campaign capable of holding together
nationalists, cultural conservatives and parts of the libertarian right. He
competes with PiS for young men and anti-establishment voters without fully
subordinating his campaign to the governing camp.

His result will determine how seriously either runoff candidate must bargain
for the radical right's endorsement—or its neutrality.

- @candidate_kosiniak: PSL remains in the field

@candidate_kosiniak
title: Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz — the local moderate
face-image: img/poland/events/pres-candidate-kosiniak.webp

**Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz — PSL chair and former labour minister**

Kosiniak-Kamysz enters with mayors, county organisations and a rural electorate
that larger parties often remember only during campaigns. He offers a moderate,
institutional candidacy grounded in PSL's local networks.

That space is disappearing around him. Duda dominates much of the countryside,
while Hołownia competes for centrist voters looking beyond the established
parties.

- @candidate_other: The smaller committees have registered too

@candidate_other
title: The smaller committees

Five further candidates complete the eleven-name ballot.


**Stanisław Żółtek**, a veteran of the Congress of the New Right, represents
the libertarian and anti-tax fringe.

**Marek Jakubiak**, businessman and leader of the Federation for the Republic,
appeals to nationalist, entrepreneurial and anti-establishment voters.

**Paweł Tanajno**, an independent entrepreneur, turns the anger of small
business owners and opponents of the lockdown restrictions into an outsider
campaign.

**Waldemar Witkowski**, a housing-cooperative manager and Labour Union
politician, offers a small but recognisably social-democratic alternative.

**Mirosław Piotrowski**, an academic standing for the Movement of True Europe,
represents the hardline Catholic-conservative fringe.

None is likely to threaten the leading candidates. Together, however, they draw
support from several constituencies that might otherwise flow toward the larger
campaigns. In a close runoff, their voters' second choices—or their refusal to
choose—may still affect the result.

- @candidate_left: And our own nominee?

@candidate_left
title: [+ presidential_candidate +] — the Left's nominee

**[+ presidential_candidate +] — Lewica's nominee**
[? if presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń": Wiosna's founder and an MEP
offers a media-facing progressive campaign.?][? if presidential_candidate =
"Adrian Zandberg": Razem's co-founder and a Sejm deputy offers a
redistributive campaign built around work and public services.?][? if
presidential_candidate = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": A Sejm deputy with an
education and social-policy profile offers a bridge between labour and younger
progressives.?][? if presidential_candidate = "Anna-Maria Żukowska": An SLD
spokeswoman and Sejm deputy offers a combative media campaign.?][? if
presidential_candidate = "Katarzyna Kotula": A Wiosna MP and equality
campaigner offers a movement-facing progressive campaign.?][? if
presidential_candidate = "Magdalena Biejat": A Razem Sejm deputy identified
with housing and social policy offers an organiser-led campaign.?]

Our candidate begins outside the runoff places. The campaign can still defend
an independent electorate, force social issues into the contest and determine
which finalist receives Left votes—and at what price.

- @candidate_alignment: Choose the Left's electoral strategy

@candidate_alignment
title: The Left chooses its line

**The field is now complete. Lewica must choose its electoral line.**

With the field mapped, the alliance must decide whether to measure its own
strength or attempt an exceptional common candidacy.

- @separate_candidate
- @joint_request

@separate_candidate
title: Fight under the Left's own colours
subtitle: Keep a distinct candidacy and let every democratic committee test its strength.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate = 0;
Q.pres_ko_joint_conversion = 0;
Q.pres_first_calc_mode = "opening_poll";
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " begins an independent first-round campaign";
!}
go-to: opening_poll

@joint_request
title: Ask KO to withdraw and back one democratic-social candidate
subtitle: Exceptional path: strong polls, trust, unity and a credible relationship are all required.
choose-if: resources >= 1 and ko_relation >= 60 and left_vote_intent >= 13 and public_trust >= 50 and party_unity >= 60 and (primary_mandate >= 28 or (presidential_candidate = "Robert Biedroń" and spring_dissent <= 15))
unavailable-subtitle: The Left lacks the leverage or legitimacy to turn KO's nomination crisis into a common ticket.
go-to: joint_terms

@joint_terms
title: The price of one democratic candidacy
new-page: true

KO will stand down only for a pact it can defend to its own voters. The choice
sets both the transfer rate and the debts carried into a possible runoff.

- @joint_social
- @joint_institutional
- @separate_candidate: End the talks and keep separate candidacies

@joint_social
title: Sign a social floor on health, housing and labour rights
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Better voter transfer; liberal and old-guard resistance.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The common campaign cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pres_ko_joint_candidate = 1; pres_ko_joint_conversion = 0.86; pres_first_calc_mode = "opening_poll"; ko_relation += 5; labor_credibility += 3; public_trust += 2; barons_dissent += 5; ko_coalition_dissent += 3; news_headline = "KO withdraws for a democratic-social common ticket"
go-to: opening_poll

@joint_institutional
title: Make it a constitutional ticket with a modest social annex
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Easier for KO; Razem sees a liberal rescue operation.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Even the joint legal operation needs staff and ballot infrastructure.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_ko_joint_candidate = 1; pres_ko_joint_conversion = 0.82; pres_first_calc_mode = "opening_poll"; ko_relation += 8; constitutional_restraint += 4; public_trust += 2; razem_dissent += 8; labor_credibility -= 2; news_headline = "KO withdraws for a common constitutional candidate"
go-to: opening_poll

@calculate_first
on-arrival: {!
const clampPres = function(value, low, high) {
    return Math.max(low, Math.min(high, Number(value) || 0));
};
const ids = [
    "duda", "trzaskowski", "holownia", "bosak",
    "kosiniak", "left", "other"
];
const raw = {
    duda:
        43.50 +
        ((Number(Q.pis_vote_intent) || 43.6) - 43.6) * 0.24 +
        (Number(Q.government_delivery) || 0) * 0.035 +
        (45 - (Number(Q.household_security) || 45)) * 0.012 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_duda) || 0),
    trzaskowski:
        30.46 +
        ((Number(Q.ko_vote_intent) || 27.4) - 27.4) * 0.24 +
        ((Number(Q.judicial_legitimacy) || 36) - 36) * 0.018 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_trzaskowski) || 0),
    holownia:
        13.87 +
        ((Number(Q.public_trust) || 43) - 43) * -0.012 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_holownia) || 0),
    bosak:
        6.78 +
        ((Number(Q.konf_vote_intent) || 6.8) - 6.8) * 0.32 +
        ((Number(Q.far_right_agenda) || 32) - 32) * 0.022 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_bosak) || 0),
    kosiniak:
        2.36 +
        ((Number(Q.psl_vote_intent) || 8.6) - 8.6) * 0.11 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_kosiniak) || 0),
    left:
        (Number(Q.presidential_candidate_base) || 2.2) +
        ((Number(Q.left_vote_intent) || 12.6) - 12.6) * 0.22 +
        ((Number(Q.party_unity) || 58) - 58) * 0.025 +
        ((Number(Q.public_trust) || 43) - 43) * 0.020 +
        ((Number(Q.media_capacity) || 16) - 16) * 0.018 +
        ((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.012 +
        ((Number(Q.primary_mandate) || 30) - 30) * 0.010 +
        (Number(Q.pres_bonus_left) || 0),
    other:
        0.81 + (Number(Q.pres_bonus_other) || 0)
};

if (Q.postal_election_stance == "Democratic legal front") {
    raw.trzaskowski += 0.25;
    raw.left += 0.10;
    raw.duda -= 0.15;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "The legal front modestly mobilises both democratic campaigns";
} else if (Q.postal_election_stance == "Gowin postponement bargain") {
    raw.duda += 0.12;
    raw.holownia += 0.10;
    raw.left -= 0.08;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "The postponement bargain rewards moderation outside the Left";
} else if (Q.postal_election_stance == "Boycott") {
    raw.left -= 0.45;
    raw.holownia += 0.12;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "The abandoned boycott line depresses Left conversion in the restored vote";
} else if (Q.postal_election_stance == "Compete and litigate") {
    raw.left += 0.25;
    Q.pres_postal_stance_effect =
        "Ballot preparation survives the legal challenge and aids the Left campaign";
}

if (Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate) {
    const displaced = Math.max(0, raw.trzaskowski);
    const conversion = clampPres(
        (Number(Q.pres_ko_joint_conversion) || 0.82) +
            ((Number(Q.ko_relation) || 60) - 60) * 0.0015 +
            ((Number(Q.party_unity) || 60) - 60) * 0.001,
        0.80,
        0.90
    );
    raw.trzaskowski = 0;
    raw.left += displaced * conversion;
    raw.holownia += displaced * 0.075;
    raw.duda += displaced * 0.025;
    raw.other += displaced * Math.max(0, 0.90 - conversion);
}

let noisePrefix = "pres_open_noise_";
if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "tracking_poll") {
    noisePrefix = "pres_track_noise_";
}
if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "first_result") {
    noisePrefix = "pres_r1_shock_";
}
for (const id of ids) {
    if (id == "trzaskowski" && Q.pres_ko_joint_candidate) {
        raw[id] = 0;
    } else {
        raw[id] = Math.max(
            id == "other" ? 0.05 : 0.15,
            raw[id] + (Number(Q[noisePrefix + id]) || 0)
        );
    }
}
const total = ids.reduce(function(sum, id) {
    return sum + raw[id];
}, 0);
const share = {};
for (const id of ids) {
    share[id] = raw[id] * 100 / Math.max(1, total);
}

const roundedShares = function(values) {
    const rounded = {};
    for (const id of ids) {
        rounded[id] = Math.round(values[id] * 10) / 10;
    }
    const roundedTotal = ids.reduce(function(sum, id) {
        return sum + rounded[id];
    }, 0);
    const residual = Math.round((100 - roundedTotal) * 10) / 10;
    let residualId = "other";
    if (rounded.other + residual < 0) {
        residualId = ids.slice().sort(function(left, right) {
            return rounded[right] - rounded[left];
        })[0];
    }
    rounded[residualId] =
        Math.round((rounded[residualId] + residual) * 10) / 10;
    return rounded;
};
const display = roundedShares(share);

if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "opening_poll" ||
    Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "tracking_poll") {
    for (const id of ids) {
        Q["pres_poll_" + id] = display[id];
    }
    if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "tracking_poll" &&
        Q.pres_debate_resolved) {
        Q.pres_debate_poll_shift =
            Math.round(
                (
                    Q.pres_poll_left -
                    (Number(Q.pres_debate_poll_before_left) || 0)
                ) * 10
            ) / 10;
    }
}

if (Q.pres_first_calc_mode == "first_result") {
    const wasNewCount = !Q.pres_first_round_complete;
    for (const id of ids) {
        Q["pres_r1_raw_" + id] = share[id];
        Q["pres_r1_display_" + id] = display[id];
    }
    const ordered = ids.filter(function(id) {
        return share[id] > 0.000001;
    }).sort(function(left, right) {
        if (Math.abs(share[right] - share[left]) > 0.0000001) {
            return share[right] - share[left];
        }
        return ids.indexOf(left) - ids.indexOf(right);
    });
    const names = {
        duda: "Andrzej Duda",
        trzaskowski: "Rafał Trzaskowski",
        holownia: "Szymon Hołownia",
        bosak: "Krzysztof Bosak",
        kosiniak: "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz",
        left: Q.presidential_candidate,
        other: "Other candidates"
    };
    Q.pres_r1_leader_key = ordered[0];
    Q.pres_r1_leader_name = names[ordered[0]];
    Q.pres_r1_runner_key = ordered[1] || ordered[0];
    Q.pres_r1_runner_name = names[Q.pres_r1_runner_key];
    Q.pres_finalist_a_key = Q.pres_r1_leader_key;
    Q.pres_finalist_a_name = Q.pres_r1_leader_name;
    Q.pres_finalist_b_key = Q.pres_r1_runner_key;
    Q.pres_finalist_b_name = Q.pres_r1_runner_name;
    Q.pres_first_round_majority =
        share[Q.pres_r1_leader_key] > 50 ? 1 : 0;

    const turnout = clampPres(
        64.51 +
            ((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.035 +
            (Number(Q.pres_turnout_bonus) || 0) * 0.18 +
            (Number(Q.pres_r1_turnout_shock) || 0),
        58,
        72
    );
    Q.pres_r1_turnout = Math.round(turnout * 100) / 100;
    Q.pres_r1_valid_votes = Math.round(
        19425459 * turnout / 64.51
    );
    const votes = {};
    let allocated = 0;
    for (const id of ids) {
        votes[id] = Math.floor(
            Q.pres_r1_valid_votes * share[id] / 100
        );
        allocated += votes[id];
    }
    votes[Q.pres_r1_leader_key] +=
        Q.pres_r1_valid_votes - allocated;
    const formatVotes = function(value) {
        return String(Math.round(value)).replace(
            /\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g,
            " "
        );
    };
    for (const id of ids) {
        Q["pres_r1_votes_" + id] = votes[id];
        Q["pres_r1_votes_" + id + "_display"] =
            formatVotes(votes[id]);
    }
    Q.pres_r1_valid_votes_display =
        formatVotes(Q.pres_r1_valid_votes);
    Q.presidential_result =
        Math.round(share.left * 100) / 100;
    Q.pres_historical_benchmark = 2.22;
    Q.pres_expected_result = Math.round(
        (
            Number.isFinite(Number(Q.pres_poll_left))
                ? Number(Q.pres_poll_left)
                : Number(Q.presidential_candidate_base) || 2.2
        ) * 100
    ) / 100;
    Q.pres_expectation_gap = Math.round(
        (Q.presidential_result - Q.pres_expected_result) * 100
    ) / 100;
    Q.pres_historical_gap = Math.round(
        (Q.presidential_result - Q.pres_historical_benchmark) * 100
    ) / 100;
    const leftTransformed =
        ordered[0] == "left" || ordered[1] == "left";
    if (leftTransformed) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Party-system transformation";
        Q.pres_performance_level = 4;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 2.5) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Shattering disaster";
        Q.pres_performance_level = -3;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 4) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Severe defeat";
        Q.pres_performance_level = -2;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 5.5) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Disappointing or ambiguous";
        Q.pres_performance_level = -1;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 7.5) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Base held; broadly satisfying";
        Q.pres_performance_level = 1;
    } else if (Q.presidential_result < 10) {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Strong result";
        Q.pres_performance_level = 2;
    } else {
        Q.pres_performance_band = "Breakthrough";
        Q.pres_performance_level = 3;
    }
    Q.pres_first_round_complete = 1;
    Q.pres_2020_phase = Q.pres_first_round_majority
        ? "Decided in the first round"
        : "Between rounds";

    if (Q.pres_first_round_majority) {
        Q.pres_runoff_winner_key = Q.pres_r1_leader_key;
        Q.pres_runoff_winner_name = Q.pres_r1_leader_name;
        Q.pres_2020_president_elect_key = Q.pres_r1_leader_key;
        Q.pres_2020_president_elect_name = Q.pres_r1_leader_name;
        Q.pres_runoff_complete = 1;
        Q.trzaskowski_won =
            Q.pres_r1_leader_key == "trzaskowski" ? 1 : 0;
        Q.left_president = 0;
        if (Q.trzaskowski_won) {
            Q.trz_inauguration_status =
                "President-elect — certification pending";
            Q.pres_2020_phase = "Certification pending";
        }
    }
    if (wasNewCount) {
        const level = Number(Q.pres_performance_level) || 0;
        const previousFailure = Q.pres_feedback_active &&
            (Number(Q.pres_feedback_direction) || 0) < 0 && level < 0;
        let duration = level == -3 || level >= 3 ? 12 :
            (level == -2 || level == 2 ? 10 :
            (level == -1 ? 7 : 8));
        let consideration = level == -3 ? -6 :
            (level == -2 ? -3.8 :
            (level == -1 ? -1.4 :
            (level == 1 ? 1.2 :
            (level == 2 ? 2.7 :
            (level == 3 ? 4.2 : 5.5)))));
        let feedbackTurnout = level == -3 ? -5 :
            (level == -2 ? -3.1 :
            (level == -1 ? -1.0 :
            (level == 1 ? 1.4 :
            (level == 2 ? 2.4 :
            (level == 3 ? 3.4 : 4.5)))));
        if (previousFailure) {
            duration = Math.min(12, duration + 2);
            consideration *= 1.15;
            feedbackTurnout *= 1.15;
            Q.pres_feedback_reinforcements =
                (Number(Q.pres_feedback_reinforcements) || 0) + 1;
        }
        const expectationAdjustment = Math.max(
            -1.5,
            Math.min(1.5, (Number(Q.pres_expectation_gap) || 0) * 0.25)
        );
        consideration += expectationAdjustment;
        feedbackTurnout += expectationAdjustment * 0.65;
        if (level == 1) {
            consideration = Math.max(0.5, consideration);
            feedbackTurnout = Math.max(0.6, feedbackTurnout);
        }
        Q.pres_feedback_active = 1;
        Q.pres_feedback_source = "2020 presidential first round";
        Q.pres_feedback_direction = level < 0 ? -1 : 1;
        Q.pres_feedback_duration = duration;
        Q.pres_feedback_months_remaining = duration;
        Q.pres_feedback_decay_factor = 1;
        Q.pres_feedback_consideration =
            Math.round(consideration * 100) / 100;
        Q.pres_feedback_turnout =
            Math.round(feedbackTurnout * 100) / 100;
        Q.pres_feedback_consideration_current =
            Q.pres_feedback_consideration;
        Q.pres_feedback_turnout_current = Q.pres_feedback_turnout;
        Q.pres_feedback_leadership_pressure = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_leadership_challenge = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_donor_loss = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_activist_loss = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_media_loss = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_faction_pressure = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_base_certainty = 0;
        Q.pres_feedback_squeeze_protection = 0;
        if (level == -3) {
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_pressure = 85;
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_challenge = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_donor_loss = 2;
            Q.pres_feedback_activist_loss = 6;
            Q.pres_feedback_media_loss = 4;
            Q.pres_feedback_faction_pressure = 8;
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = 6;
            Q.resources -= 2;
            Q.organiser_energy -= 6;
            Q.media_capacity -= 4;
            Q.media_access -= 5;
            Q.leadership_authority -= 9;
            Q.list_confidence -= 8;
            Q.winner_reputation -= 7;
            Q.electoral_viability -= 5;
            Q.party_unity -= 7;
            Q.barons_dissent += 7;
            Q.spring_dissent += 8;
            Q.labor_dissent += 5;
            Q.progressives_dissent += 7;
            Q.razem_dissent += 6;
        } else if (level == -2) {
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_pressure = 65;
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_challenge = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_donor_loss = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_activist_loss = 4;
            Q.pres_feedback_media_loss = 3;
            Q.pres_feedback_faction_pressure = 6;
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = 4;
            Q.resources -= 1;
            Q.organiser_energy -= 4;
            Q.media_capacity -= 3;
            Q.media_access -= 3;
            Q.leadership_authority -= 6;
            Q.list_confidence -= 5;
            Q.winner_reputation -= 4;
            Q.electoral_viability -= 3;
            Q.party_unity -= 5;
            Q.barons_dissent += 5;
            Q.spring_dissent += 6;
            Q.labor_dissent += 3;
            Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
            Q.razem_dissent += 4;
        } else if (level == -1) {
            Q.pres_feedback_leadership_pressure = 30;
            Q.pres_feedback_activist_loss = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_media_loss = 1;
            Q.pres_feedback_faction_pressure = 2;
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight = 1;
            Q.organiser_energy -= 1;
            Q.media_capacity -= 1;
            Q.media_access -= 1;
            Q.leadership_authority -= 2;
            Q.list_confidence -= 2;
            Q.winner_reputation -= 1;
            Q.party_unity -= 2;
            Q.spring_dissent += 2;
            Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
            Q.razem_dissent += 1;
        } else {
            Q.pres_feedback_base_certainty = level == 1 ? 65 :
                (level == 2 ? 78 : 92);
            Q.pres_feedback_squeeze_protection = 1;
            Q.party_unity += level == 1 ? 3 : (level == 2 ? 4 : 6);
            Q.organiser_energy += level == 1 ? 2 : (level == 2 ? 3 : 5);
            Q.media_capacity += level == 1 ? 1 : (level == 2 ? 2 : 4);
            Q.media_access += level == 1 ? 1 : (level == 2 ? 2 : 4);
            Q.leadership_authority += level == 1 ? 3 :
                (level == 2 ? 4 : 6);
            Q.list_confidence += level == 1 ? 5 :
                (level == 2 ? 6 : 8);
            Q.winner_reputation += level == 1 ? 2 :
                (level == 2 ? 4 : 6);
            Q.electoral_viability += level == 1 ? 2 :
                (level == 2 ? 3 : 5);
            Q.tactical_desertion_to_ko = Math.max(
                0,
                Q.tactical_desertion_to_ko - (level == 1 ? 2 : 4)
            );
            Q.tactical_desertion_to_abstention = Math.max(
                0,
                Q.tactical_desertion_to_abstention - (level == 1 ? 1 : 3)
            );
            Q.barons_dissent -= level == 1 ? 1 : 2;
            Q.spring_dissent -= level == 1 ? 1 : 2;
            Q.progressives_dissent -= level == 1 ? 1 : 2;
        }
        Q.pres_feedback_tactical_current =
            Q.pres_feedback_tactical_flight;
        const holowniaResult = Math.max(
            0,
            Number(Q.pres_r1_display_holownia) ||
                Number(Q.pres_poll_holownia) || 0
        );
        const p2050Conversion = Math.max(
            0.25,
            Math.min(5, (holowniaResult - 2) * 0.32)
        );
        Q.p2050_emerged = 1;
        Q.p2050_relation = Math.max(
            Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0,
            Math.round(18 + Math.min(18, holowniaResult * 0.75))
        );
        Q.p2050_leader = "Szymon Hołownia";
        Q.p2050_poll_momentum =
            (Number(Q.p2050_poll_momentum) || 0) + p2050Conversion;
        Q.ko_poll_momentum =
            (Number(Q.ko_poll_momentum) || 0) - p2050Conversion * 0.55;
        Q.psl_poll_momentum =
            (Number(Q.psl_poll_momentum) || 0) - p2050Conversion * 0.15;
        Q.other_poll_momentum =
            (Number(Q.other_poll_momentum) || 0) - p2050Conversion * 0.20;
    }
    Q.news_headline = Q.pres_first_round_majority
        ? Q.pres_r1_leader_name +
            " wins the presidency in the first round"
        : Q.pres_r1_leader_name + " and " +
            Q.pres_r1_runner_name + " enter the runoff";
}
!}

@opening_poll
title: The opening tracking poll
new-page: true
call: poland_presidential_election.calculate_first

= A race with error bars

The poll has a **±1.8 point working margin**. It is sampled from the same party,
trust, organisation and turnout state used by the wider electorate model.

Postal-election carryover: **[+ pres_postal_stance_effect +]**.

<div class="poll-table">
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-pis"><b>Duda</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_duda +]%</span><span>PiS</span></div>
[? if pres_ko_joint_candidate = 0: <div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-ko"><b>Trzaskowski</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_trzaskowski +]%</span><span>KO</span></div>?]
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-p2050"><b>Hołownia</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_holownia +]%</span><span>civic campaign</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-konf"><b>Bosak</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_bosak +]%</span><span>Konf.</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-psl"><b>Kosiniak-Kamysz</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_kosiniak +]%</span><span>PSL</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span class="party party-lewica"><b>[+ presidential_candidate +]</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_left +]%</span><span>[? if pres_ko_joint_candidate: common ticket?][? if pres_ko_joint_candidate = 0: Left?]</span></div>
<div class="poll-row"><span><b>Other</b></span><span>[+ pres_poll_other +]%</span><span>combined</span></div>
</div>

- @campaign_menu: Open the two-move campaign board

@campaign_menu
title: Two moves before the first ballot
new-page: true

= Campaign board — [+ pres_first_actions_remaining +] moves remain

Each operation can be used once. Polling measures the field; it does not reveal
the saved election-day shock.

- @campaign_digital
- @campaign_work
- @campaign_equality
- @campaign_counties
- @campaign_constitution
- @campaign_insurgent

@campaign_digital
title: Buy reach: video, targeting and rapid response
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Strongest where a media operation already exists.
view-if: pres_campaign_digital = 0
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The campaign lacks cash and production capacity.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pres_campaign_digital = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.95 + media_capacity * 0.004; media_capacity += 3; pres_turnout_bonus += 0.4; news_headline = "The Left buys a professional digital finish"
go-to: campaign_menu if pres_first_actions_remaining > 0; debate if pres_first_actions_remaining <= 0

@campaign_work
title: Put work, rent and public health on every podium
subtitle: Free. Distinctive first-round ownership; KO dislikes the contrast.
view-if: pres_campaign_work = 0
on-arrival: pres_campaign_work = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.85; labor_credibility += 4; workers_support += 2; public_sector_support += 2; razem_dissent -= 3; ko_relation -= 2; news_headline = "The presidential campaign becomes a social argument"
go-to: campaign_menu if pres_first_actions_remaining > 0; debate if pres_first_actions_remaining <= 0

@campaign_equality
title: Give women and equality movements the closing week
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Mobilisation with a conservative-caucus price.
view-if: pres_campaign_equality = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The campaign cannot support the organising network.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_campaign_equality = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.82; feminist_trust += 5; women_support += 3; young_support += 2; pres_turnout_bonus += 0.6; barons_dissent += 5; news_headline = "Equality movements enter the presidential ground campaign"
go-to: campaign_menu if pres_first_actions_remaining > 0; debate if pres_first_actions_remaining <= 0

@campaign_counties
title: Trade studio time for a county-by-county tour
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Local reach and a small opening among PSL voters.
view-if: pres_campaign_counties = 0
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Too few buses, organisers and county offices are available.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_campaign_counties = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.72; pres_bonus_kosiniak -= 0.10; local_network += 4; rural_support += 2; pres_turnout_bonus += 0.35; psl_relation += 2; news_headline = "The candidate leaves Warsaw for the county map"
go-to: campaign_menu if pres_first_actions_remaining > 0; debate if pres_first_actions_remaining <= 0

@campaign_constitution
title: Build the democratic-constitutional front early
subtitle: Free. Weaker first-round distinction; stronger runoff bridges.
view-if: pres_campaign_constitution = 0
on-arrival: pres_campaign_constitution = 1; pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_bonus_left += 0.48; pres_bonus_trzaskowski += 0.12 if pres_ko_joint_candidate = 0; pres_runoff_preparation += 0.55; ko_relation += 5; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 2; razem_dissent += 4; news_headline = "The campaign rehearses a democratic runoff coalition"
go-to: campaign_menu if pres_first_actions_remaining > 0; debate if pres_first_actions_remaining <= 0

@campaign_insurgent
title: Turn the nominee loose on an improvised insurgent tour
subtitle: Free fallback. Candidate visibility without a durable machine.
view-if: pres_campaign_insurgent = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_campaign_insurgent = 1;
Q.pres_first_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_bonus_left +=
    0.52 + (Number(Q.presidential_candidate_base) || 0) * 0.05;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
Q.organiser_energy -= 2;
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.news_headline =
    Q.presidential_candidate + " runs outside the headquarters script";
!}
go-to: campaign_menu if pres_first_actions_remaining > 0; debate if pres_first_actions_remaining <= 0

@debate
# prose-audit: Grade A — The debate follows the actual format in a fixed sequence, gives every possible Lewica nominee a distinct voice and permits replies from the candidate's own clock without inventing formal rebuttals.
title: The last national debate
new-page: true
on-arrival: pres_first_calc_mode = "tracking_poll"
call: poland_presidential_election.calculate_first

= 17 June 2020 — TVP, Warsaw

All eleven candidates receive the same five one-minute questions and one free
closing minute. TVP permits no formal rebuttals, but it cannot stop a candidate
from using their own clock to answer another lectern.

Rather than repeat six timers, the campaign treats the broadcast as three
linked decisions. Each choice sets how **[+ presidential_candidate +]** joins
two answers into one argument—and whether to spend precious seconds replying
directly to a rival.

[? if presidential_candidate = "Adrian Zandberg": Zandberg has already shown
that a crowded television debate can change how a national audience sees him.
The campaign expects more than survival.?]

- @debate_begin: Take the Left's lectern

@debate_begin
title: Take the Left's lectern
on-arrival: {!
if (!Q.pres_debate_initialized) {
    Q.pres_debate_initialized = 1;
    Q.pres_debate_poll_before_left =
        Number(Q.pres_poll_left) || 0;
    Q.pres_debate_stops_remaining = 3;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The full presidential field enters TVP's final debate";

    const voices = {
        "Robert Biedroń": {
            frame: [
                "Defend asylum law and a secular school without apology",
                "Answer Duda: neither refugees nor pupils need PiS permission",
                "Lead with controlled asylum and freedom of conscience"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Make equal families and evidence-led vaccination one promise",
                "Answer Bosak: my family is not your campaign prop",
                "Promise partnerships now and build trust before vaccine rules"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close on an open Poland where every family belongs",
                "Answer Duda with the citizens his presidency left outside",
                "Challenge Hołownia: change needs more than a new face"
            ]
        },
        "Adrian Zandberg": {
            frame: [
                "Put a capable secular state above bishops and border panic",
                "Answer Duda: strength is law and capacity, not scapegoats",
                "Reject forced quotas and move religion outside public school"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Join equal dignity to a universal public-health service",
                "Answer Bosak: rights do not close wards; underfunding does",
                "Secure civil rights while keeping the vaccine mandate cautious"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close on wages, rents and a social republic",
                "Answer Duda with five years of signatures against working people",
                "Challenge Hołownia: the duopoly is economic, not only partisan"
            ]
        },
        "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": {
            frame: [
                "Defend the secular classroom as a common public institution",
                "Answer Duda: public schools cannot sort children by belief",
                "Protect secular access while leaving religion to families"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Pair equal family law with trusted, universal vaccination",
                "Answer Bosak: public safety needs trust, not scapegoats",
                "Set a rights floor and earn consent through public health"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close on schools, hospitals and dignified work",
                "Answer Duda with the public institutions weakened on his watch",
                "Challenge Hołownia to say who pays for political renewal"
            ]
        },
        "Anna-Maria Żukowska": {
            frame: [
                "Reject both loaded premises before the clock can trap you",
                "Answer Duda directly and name the diversion",
                "Give a clipped defence of controlled asylum and voluntary religion"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Say yes to equal families and science—without qualifications",
                "Turn Bosak's culture-war premise back on him",
                "Defend partnerships and voluntary vaccination in one sharp line"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close with the line every studio will have to replay",
                "Put Duda's record on trial, signature by signature",
                "Tell Hołownia that a new logo is not a new politics"
            ]
        },
        "Katarzyna Kotula": {
            frame: [
                "Speak for pupils and families excluded by the Church's rules",
                "Answer Duda with the people his politics pushes outside",
                "Make religion voluntary and equal treatment non-negotiable"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Demand full family equality and vaccination led by evidence",
                "Answer Bosak with the families he would deny",
                "Protect partnerships now and organise for the rest"
            ],
            close: [
                "Give women and equality movements the final minute",
                "Answer Duda with five years of blocked rights",
                "Challenge Hołownia to choose a side on equality"
            ]
        },
        "Magdalena Biejat": {
            frame: [
                "Ground solidarity in the everyday security of every family",
                "Answer Duda: security begins with homes, not exclusion",
                "Tie controlled reception and voluntary religion to local capacity"
            ],
            rights: [
                "Make family security mean equal law and accessible vaccination",
                "Answer Bosak with care work, rent and real family life",
                "Win partnerships and build vaccination through neighbourhood trust"
            ],
            close: [
                "Close on rent, care and the homes people can afford",
                "Answer Duda with the families his economic record squeezed",
                "Challenge Hołownia: renewal without social guarantees is branding"
            ]
        }
    };
    const voice = voices[Q.presidential_candidate] || voices["Robert Biedroń"];
    Q.pres_debate_frame_signature_title = voice.frame[0];
    Q.pres_debate_frame_reply_title = voice.frame[1];
    Q.pres_debate_frame_cautious_title = voice.frame[2];
    Q.pres_debate_rights_signature_title = voice.rights[0];
    Q.pres_debate_rights_reply_title = voice.rights[1];
    Q.pres_debate_rights_cautious_title = voice.rights[2];
    Q.pres_debate_close_signature_title = voice.close[0];
    Q.pres_debate_close_duda_title = voice.close[1];
    Q.pres_debate_close_holownia_title = voice.close[2];
}
!}
go-to: debate_frame

@debate_frame
title: Refugees and First Communion
subtitle: Foreign policy and the place of religion in public schools.
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
view-if: pres_debate_frame_done = 0

The moderator moves from compulsory refugee relocation to preparing children
for First Communion during religion lessons. These are separate one-minute
answers; the political test is whether they sound like the same candidate.

Duda has already cast both questions as matters of national control and
parental choice. There is no rebuttal bell, but **[+ presidential_candidate +]**
may use part of either answer to challenge his frame.

- @debate_frame_direct
- @debate_frame_material
- @debate_frame_reassure

@debate_frame_direct
